<title>NIGERIA: Julius Berger 1996 pre-tax up, div steady.</title>
<headline>Julius Berger 1996 pre-tax up, div steady.</headline>
<dateline>LAGOS 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year result for Nigeria's biggest construction company Julius Berger Plc to end-December 1996.</p>
<p>		     (In million naira unless stated)</p>
<p>					1996	 1995</p>
<p>Turnover			    5,600 vs 4,100</p>
<p>Profit before taxation	  205.4 vs 158.3</p>
<p>Taxation			     47.9 vs 43.8</p>
<p>Profit after taxation	   157.5 vs 114.4</p>
<p> Dividend per share	   30 kobo vs 30 kobo</p>
<p>Payment date September 19, 1997. NOTE: Julius Berger is 60 percent Nigerian-owned and 40 percent by Germany's Bilfinger and Berger Bau AG.</p>
<p>($1=85 naira)</p>
<p>-- Lagos newsroom +234 1 263 03 17</p>
</text>
